  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Parents",
      "h2": "Mother & Father",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>La mere</strong> = mother, <strong>le pere</strong> = father. The informal <strong>maman</strong> and <strong>papa</strong> mean mum and dad — used at home with family.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Sibs",
      "h2": "Brothers & Sisters",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Le frere</strong> = brother. <strong>La soeur</strong> = sister. To talk about more than one: <strong>les freres</strong>, <strong>les soeurs</strong>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Have",
      "h2": "Saying You Have",
      "body_html": "<p>Use <strong>J'ai</strong> = I have. 'J'ai un frere et deux soeurs' = 'I have one brother and two sisters'. Number first, then person.</p>"
    }
  ],
